#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/0d06481c63a618262b9034124c24cd1d0c566ee9d6b891fa470e09dc67f5f6c6.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/104c591a6a72cf3caab1bc2a965c57258bb37a31578254696e0c1cd740fe5915.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/e008383384401198e67f648cce33a720d98afb6a6f60a14ba7ffa21dcc095a5f.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/c85e33202a691b685431ac16efab6a7fd932eac056743df6e81632587f0465b2.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7070e989-c302-5af5-85f8-1e38e0014a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330317} {:answer/id #uuid "e576cf28-423c-563b-9e57-2ef308902b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-7,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330318} {:answer/id #uuid "a40bc766-b4f8-537b-9d5a-a11eff851db2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=-5,\\,c=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330319} {:answer/id #uuid "40655041-f289-502a-9ea2-871995a7eeab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330320} {:answer/id #uuid "5df9f508-b858-5678-a4ae-e472f4e46b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=-1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40655041-f289-502a-9ea2-871995a7eeab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330320} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8f1c6a1-1a09-556a-a7fa-a22787f05e4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e2fbe52-d918-52c4-aea4-f6898d19b9a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130535" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+z=1 \\\\ -x-3y+9z=-2 \\\\ 4x-7y-z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & c \\\\ -1 & b & 9 \\\\ a & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd6aaf3-2f2b-5b4e-9a66-8e97e1dc63d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330324} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ba4a9f-e65a-5490-ac8f-28df29be2287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330325} {:answer/id #uuid "a73157f4-b120-5860-8093-087aee68e1fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330326} {:answer/id #uuid "de515c60-ce9c-5b30-a66e-1f60183adff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=8,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330327} {:answer/id #uuid "4befcde8-81c2-5d6a-a25a-429241bec310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=8,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8ba4a9f-e65a-5490-ac8f-28df29be2287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330325} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddaa1d36-3be6-53f0-83e1-f0abbc7f9daa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2ddb9ae-e08d-5346-95be-8df31e1fb92f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130536" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea142ec8-5dd7-5a9b-9e06-dcdb6db57742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=5,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330331} {:answer/id #uuid "25e57de6-3fc4-5fa7-af00-5f628060c8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=1,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330332} {:answer/id #uuid "df0ca58e-cc2e-51e6-91ce-63f4ad40ee6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-7,\\,b=1,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330333} {:answer/id #uuid "1df6607c-5133-5d94-85c7-8a04d4fab857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330334} {:answer/id #uuid "02238340-e005-5423-8044-8e5905140f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-7,\\,c=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1df6607c-5133-5d94-85c7-8a04d4fab857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330334} :answer-field/id #uuid "247f7b3a-42e3-5c20-a1dc-8036e2c18eba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f48fae54-75c1-5735-95b2-656baa979098" :question/math-academy-id "q-130562" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}z-7x-5=0 \\\\ 4y-x-3z-2=0 \\\\ 2y+x-8=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & a \\\\ b & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-7x+0y+z=5 \\\\ -x+4y-3z=2 \\\\ x+2y+0z=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a06272f1-09a1-5cce-8677-dc083ac5d764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330338} {:answer/id #uuid "9f25993d-ae7b-5da6-a4d1-7978da5a4184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a06272f1-09a1-5cce-8677-dc083ac5d764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330338} :answer-field/id #uuid "702a739e-5086-5ea9-b0a9-b90d58ecd33c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f41715-2c7e-5689-9722-da15011365a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02f41715-2c7e-5689-9722-da15011365a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/