x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=11 \\\\ -x-3y-z=0 \\\\ 8x+6y+3z=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f87dd92a-95f5-5bc1-ac33-1c9ab1aa25c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284647} {:answer/id #uuid "f05b4508-334e-5647-ac52-1c34d77ffe58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f05b4508-334e-5647-ac52-1c34d77ffe58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284648} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdf780d9-b415-5718-ad58-68c1088122c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9437d0b-b101-59cd-a076-a9d6a69a5f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9437d0b-b101-59cd-a076-a9d6a69a5f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284650} :answer-field/id #uuid "b22341ac-f523-5fc6-a2fa-17463c32970f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d57c071e-1253-5179-8885-810c499209f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d57c071e-1253-5179-8885-810c499209f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284652} :answer-field/id #uuid "6617570b-31ce-518c-bb86-beff57a80369" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284651} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7e9163d-91b5-589a-b7fa-e5bde257012e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7e9163d-91b5-589a-b7fa-e5bde257012e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284654} :answer-field/id #uuid "8012b573-d9b4-5ed7-87ed-5a0cdec76e3a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb147a5b-b254-59ff-ab9f-0e3ee4e488bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-316985" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z=6 \\\\ y-9z=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-2$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $6$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z=6 \\\\ 0x+y-9z=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4c451a8-55cd-54b5-8793-c30fe141cb14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 11, b =-4, c = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058154} {:answer/id #uuid "f113ab79-881c-543e-8611-e41bf9458cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b =-6, c = 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058155} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e0a939-4d5b-57e6-aa68-2df14d854d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a =-4, b =-4, c = 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058156} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe7bdf3-c649-58c5-9f73-a0500f16314c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b = 11, c =-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058157} {:answer/id #uuid "765d9c43-743e-5663-a87f-f9bf5818a214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b =-6, c = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f113ab79-881c-543e-8611-e41bf9458cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b =-6, c = 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058155} :answer-field/id #uuid "71566df2-83fb-56af-976b-7a9a5cafae50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5006a5f1-0a5e-50bb-a47b-7da41b1e709f" :question/math-academy-id "q-36181" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "538fbde5-1162-5daf-8bd0-e7ccef9d69fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330348} {:answer/id #uuid "cbde8509-210d-5fc0-bb19-3f232d3afe82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330349} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ba78a4-e97a-5eea-a942-6f5134e65120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=5,\\,b=-6,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330350} {:answer/id #uuid "af7791f2-c22b-5ab3-acbc-af400f2443ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330351} {:answer/id #uuid "560503e3-a79a-59b9-b5cc-8f1f89efc477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-6,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbde8509-210d-5fc0-bb19-3f232d3afe82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330349} :answer-field/id #uuid "98b457cf-955c-5930-a516-c09b245c49d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "878ded7e-cbaa-5e72-af33-efae3a58cd80" :question/math-academy-id "q-75490" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+5x=3z+2 \\\\ 3x-6y=5 \\\\ 2x-3y+5z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & a & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & b \\\\ 2 & c & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y-3z=2 \\\\ 3x-6y+0z=5 \\\\ 2x-3y+5z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c40ca1b0-67c1-561c-a22a-9a93dfd65436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=5,\\,b=7,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330355} {:answer/id #uuid "79d631a6-35af-52c3-9f71-b3d77d196ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330356} {:answer/id #uuid "002f5a7f-bdee-5584-9267-990d5e06cd36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=5,\\,b=7,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330357} {:answer/id #uuid "91dc011f-db8a-53eb-b3f0-e6008cc2e9cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330358} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fc01a3-ba13-53d6-baea-5bbefed62ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79d631a6-35af-52c3-9f71-b3d77d196ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330356} :answer-field/id #uuid "60dd77f0-6d94-51ef-8243-34d4f987d473" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7bbe001-db69-5932-b577-7365e9bf59b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-75501" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5y-3z+x=2 \\\\ 3z+7x-2y=5 \\\\ 2x-2y=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & b & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ 7x-2y+3z=5 \\\\ 2x-2y+0z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b31de5b2-7a6d-5062-bc51-42b00b7f4177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=3,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330362} {:answer/id #uuid "14eda18f-60c4-5bb6-89b2-943492d84cd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330363} {:answer/id #uuid "7df89ebb-28ee-54be-a430-77ab0082f724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=2,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330364} {:answer/id #uuid "0517588e-0f70-5423-9db8-538db2d43645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=3,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330365} {:answer/id #uuid "c629a8e5-fc5f-5681-bd3e-17233c46dd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c629a8e5-fc5f-5681-bd3e-17233c46dd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330366} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cab7092-514d-569a-a3cb-86ddcdbf4c54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2fb4b6fc-e7f5-535e-a41e-aecc915867f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75511" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y+z=-1 \\\\ z+3x-2y=3 \\\\ -y+2z-x=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & b & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y+z=-1 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=3 \\\\ -x-y+2z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614d19c8-9998-5a5e-b557-ba50f566abcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330369} {:answer/id #uuid "18f9f8f7-0fbb-50f8-8960-e3feefaeaf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330370} {:answer/id #uuid "1edcddf3-971a-5fa8-a22d-9e57a1a2245f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=5,\\,b=4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330371} {:answer/id #uuid "49414cb7-7641-5475-8b14-0104ac5e4734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-5,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330372} {:answer/id #uuid "88ba2c9a-e82c-503e-9b2c-eac9f24df940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-5,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18f9f8f7-0fbb-50f8-8960-e3feefaeaf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330370} :answer-field/id #uuid "af2b5a8d-a99b-594c-a3fb-95853ef62c2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a147cf2-1edd-5a7f-9f80-a95a1f3975b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75512" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2z+x-5y=1 \\\\ -y+5z-4x=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & a \\\\ b & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & c & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-5y-2z=1 \\\\ -4x-y+5z=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6.$"}]}
